      "index": "cHoi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1948155446,
      "version": 388,
      "versionNonce": 955074952,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785228333542,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- it's a layer 4 (Transport Layer) protocol\n- Data Unit is called as Datagram\n- We have concept of PORTs to access proccesses in the host\n- it's a stateless protocol- Does not require connection establishment (Unlike TCP's 3 way Handshake)\n- Very simple protocol for communication\n- Header size of the UDP datagram is only 8 bytes",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- it's a layer 4 (Transport Layer) protocol\n- Data Unit is called as Datagram\n- We have concept of PORTs to access proccesses in the host\n- it's a stateless protocol- Does not require connection establishment (Unlike TCP's 3 way Handshake)\n- Very simple protocol for communication\n- Header size of the UDP datagram is only 8 bytes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
